  "type": "multiple-choice",
  "originalQuery": "Your company requires a high availability database setup in Cloud SQL to minimize downtime and data loss during a zonal outage. The database must automatically recover and handle write operations during failover. What is the best approach to achieve this?",
  "originalOptions": "A. Configure High Availability (HA) for the Cloud SQL instance to enable automatic failover to a standby replica in a different zone.<br/>B. Enable cross-region replication and use a read replica as the primary database during outages.<br/>C. Deploy a Cloud SQL instance with automated backups and restore the database in another zone during an outage.<br/>D. Use a multi-region Cloud Spanner instance to provide high availability and durability.",
  "domain": "Deploy scalable and highly available databases in Google Cloud",
  "hasImage": false,
